\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \xpg@aux {}{english}\ignorespaces Algorithm comparison on 196 biomedical queries, 5,035-document pool. B1 is the standard RAG baseline (rank by cosine distance to query $Q$). H1 hybrid score: $\text  {score}(d) = \alpha \cdot \text  {sim}(d,Q) + (1-\alpha ) \cdot \text  {sim}(d,C)$. H2 is identical to B1 because no ties exist in floating-point cosine distances. H3 restricts candidates to the top-$k$ by $d(Q)$, then reranks within the window by $d(C)$.}}{15}{table.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{tab:results}{{1}{15}{\texorpdfstring {\xpg@aux {\xpg@current@opts }{\languagename }}{}\ignorespaces Algorithm comparison on 196 biomedical queries, 5,035-document pool. B1 is the standard RAG baseline (rank by cosine distance to query $Q$). H1 hybrid score: $\text {score}(d) = \alpha \cdot \text {sim}(d,Q) + (1-\alpha ) \cdot \text {sim}(d,C)$. H2 is identical to B1 because no ties exist in floating-point cosine distances. H3 restricts candidates to the top-$k$ by $d(Q)$, then reranks within the window by $d(C)$}{table.caption.3}{}}
